      "content": "it's hard to see it that way when the damage feels so permanent. like, if a person is a part of a beautiful tapestry but they're the one thread that's frayed and discolored, doesn't the whole thing look broken because of them? sometimes it feels like the most selfless thing a person can do isn't to stay and struggle, but to just... step out of the way so the rest of the picture can be perfect again. wouldn't it be more honorable to leave on my own terms rather than let the rot spread?",
